*Template.net* is an AI-powered browser-based content creation platform serving 10M+ users, offering collaborative editors for graphics, documents, and whiteboards.

- Developed and maintained *backend services* using *NestJS*, *PostgreSQL*, *MongoDB*, *Redis*, and *Docker*.
- Designed and implemented *RESTful APIs* to support core application features and business logic.
- Implemented *microservices architecture* using *NestJS* and *message queues* for reliable asynchronous processing.
- Applied the *Transactional Outbox Pattern* to improve message delivery reliability and data consistency.
- Optimized *API performance* by reducing response latency and improving database query efficiency.
- Implemented *Redis caching* to reduce database load and improve API response times.
- Integrated *OpenSearch* to enable efficient search with *full-text search*, filtering, and relevance-based results.
- Applied *application security best practices*, including authentication, authorization, input validation, and rate limiting.
- Implemented *real-time collaboration* using *WebSockets* to support multi-user editing.
- Containerized backend services using *Docker* and setup deployment workflows with Github Actions.
- Monitored *API performance metrics* to identify bottlenecks, troubleshoot issues, and improve system reliability.
- Collaborated with *cross-functional teams* to deliver reliable end-to-end backend features.
- Leveraged *AI-assisted development tools*, including *GitHub Copilot* and *Claude Code*, to accelerate development and improve code quality.

